# Accounts management profile

Resume: `@accounts$` / `$accounts-profile$`.

Owner (Oct 29 2026): "Accounts will be provided later. Create a mgmt profile to configure accounts via seeding."

## Files

| File | Git | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `config/accounts-profile.example.json` | committed | Every field: description, where to get it, secret yes/no, format, target, whether code reads it today. Values empty. Regenerate with `--write-example` after editing the catalog (a test fails otherwise). |
| `config/accounts-profile.local.json` | **gitignored** (`config/*.local.json`) | Owner's copy with real values. Never commit, never paste into chat. |
| `scripts/seed-accounts-profile.js` | committed | Catalog (source of truth for target / secret / format), validator, masked plan, applier. |
| `scripts/seed-accounts-profile.test.js` | committed | `node --test scripts/seed-accounts-profile.test.js` — validation, masking, no secret in argv / logs / Firestore, env merge, example parity. No network. Lives outside `functions/` so `check-functions-sync.js` is unaffected. |

## Owner flow

1. `copy config\accounts-profile.example.json config\accounts-profile.local.json`, fill `value` for the accounts you have (empty = skip; empty never clears an existing secret), set `manual.*.value` to `true` after each Console step.
2. `node scripts/seed-accounts-profile.js` — dry run (default): validates and prints a plan with secrets masked (`••••` + last 4 when ≥ 16 chars, else `•••• (set)`) plus the Console-only checklist. Exit 1 on any invalid value. `--only twilio,stripe` limits the run.
3. `node scripts/seed-accounts-profile.js --apply --confirm-project shoutoutdemo-5b402` — writes, then redeploy the affected Functions from a clean `origin/main` export (copy `functions/.env` into the export — it is gitignored, so `git archive` does not carry it).

## Targets (only the catalog decides; metadata in the local file is ignored)

| Target | How | Secret? |
|---|---|---|
| `firebaseSecret` | `firebase functions:secrets:set NAME --project P --non-interactive`, value on **stdin** (never argv) | yes |
| `githubSecret` | `gh secret set NAME --repo jadzadco/shoutout-demo`, stdin (Azure SWA deploy token) | yes |
| `functionsEnv` | Replace / append only that key in `functions/.env` (other lines untouched; plain `process.env`, never `defineString`) | no |
| `firestoreDoc` | `platformAccountsProfile/publicConfig` (Admin SDK) — non-secret identifiers only; secret-looking values (`sk_`/`rk_`/`whsec_`/`SG.`/PEM) are rejected | no |
| manual | Console step; recorded only as `0\|1` | — |

Status doc `platformAccountsProfile/current`: `{profileVersion, updatedAtMs, updatedBy, accounts: {id: {configured 0|1, fields: {key: {set, target, secret, last4?}}, manual: {key: 0|1}, updatedAtMs}}}`. `configured = 1` only when every required field is set **and** every manual step is ticked. Accounts not in this run keep their previous status; a failed secret write is not marked set. No rules change: the collection has no client rule, so only Admin SDK reads it (a Master Admin UI would need a callable).

Credentials: Admin SDK uses `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` if set, else a temporary ADC built from the Firebase CLI login (same pattern as `seed-temp-qa-venues.js`), deleted afterwards.

